  "caption": "Cantonese Dixieland jazz band, New Orleans style with collective improvisation. Clarinet weaving fast runs above the melody, trombone with slurred tailgate glissandos, cornet leading the head with a bright brassy tone, banjo strumming steady four-beat chords, tuba walking a bouncy two-beat bass, washboard brushing a shuffle. Live-room band recording, close acoustic horns, light tape warmth. Male warm baritone, bright conversational swing delivery, melody clearly sung. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 112 BPM, B-flat major. Jaunty, warm, playful mood. No rap, no autotune, no electronic drums, no synth pop sound, no distorted guitar, no orchestral strings.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n我畫地圖 畀城市起名\n每條街 每個角 都要寫清楚\n鉛筆 間尺 加墨水\n七百條巷 我行晒\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n但有條巷 得三步闊\n我寫咗又擦 擦咗又寫\n\n[Chorus]\n無名嗰條巷 我留低空白\n地圖印出嚟 冇人知\n但你記得 嗰日落雨\n我哋喺度 共一把遮\n\n[Verse]\n老闆話 空白好浪費\n客人睇圖 要搵到路\n我話呢條 唔使搵到\n淨係要 有人行過\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我加咗個 細細嘅點\n當作一粒圖釘\n\n[Chorus]\n無名嗰條巷 我留低空白\n老闆睇到 搖頭笑\n但你記得 嗰日落雨\n我哋喺度 共一把遮\n\n[Verse]\n今朝印刷廠 送嚟樣辦\n一千張 攤開成地\n我逐張數 個細點\n一張都冇漏\n\n[Bridge]\n第日你拎住 張地圖\n行入去 搵唔到名\n但你會停低 望一望\n\n[Chorus]\n無名嗰條巷 我留低空白\n你拎住地圖 行到嗰度\n我企喺巷口 等你\n落唔落雨 都共一把遮\n\n[Outro]\n三步闊嘅巷\n夠兩個人",
